    "millsfield:images_texts": [
      "757\nSafety Instructions\nInstructions de Sécurité\nInstrucciones de Seguridad\nUS AIRWAYS",
      "EVACUATION PROCEDURES\nPROCEDIMIENTOS DE EVACUACION\nOXYGEN\nPROCEDURES D'EVACUATION\nA\nRESTRICTIONS\nRESTRICCIONES\nEXIT\nEXIT\nEXIT\nEX\n2 -\nB\nTAKEOFF/LANDING\nDESPEGUF ATERRITAIF\nBRACE POSITIONS\nPOS CIONES PARA PROTECCION\nPOSITIONS DE PROTFCTION\nOXYGENE\nINTERDICTIONS\nExit Row Seating.\n• Si usted está sentado en una fila de salida, y no\npuede leer, hablar o entender inglés, sirvase contactar a\nun representante de US Airways para que se le cambie\nde asiento.\nSi vous êtes assis près d'une issue de secours, et\nvous n'êtes pas en mesure de lire l'anglais, ni de le\nparler ou de le comprendre, veillez contacter un\nreprésentant de la compagnie US Airways pour obtenir\nun autre siede\nIf you are seated in an exit row, please review the following.\nFederal Aviation Regulations require that passengers\nseated in this row meet the selection criteria and are\nwilling and able to operate the exit and assist others in\nthe event of an emerdency in which a crewmember is\nnot available to do so. Please identify the exit nearest\nto you ana review the corresponding tandoors found dr\nthis \"Safety Instuctions\" card.\nPlease contact your Flight Attendant for reseating if you have\na condition, which is not apparent, that would prevent vou\nfrom performing the functions shown on this \"Safety\nInstructions\" card: would be harmed from doina so: do\nnot wish to do so; or if any of the following apply:\n• Mobility, strength or dexterity in both arms and hands,\nand both leas is not sufficient to perform the functions\nand assist others, including:\n-Reaching the exit quickly\n-Reaching in every direction for mechanisms used\n- Operating the exit\n- Securing the exit open\n-Removing obstructions\n(maintaining balance while doing so)\n-Quickly passing through the exit\n• You are less than 15 years old, require assistance from\nsomeone else to pertorm one or more or the unctions\nor would be prevented from doing so because of a\ncondition or responsibility, such as caring for a small\nchild.\n• You cannot sutticiently impart intormation orally to\nothers or understand oral crew commands.\n• Yoll cannot read or linderstand the written and arannic\ninstructions provided or require assistance (other than\na hearing aid to hear or understand instructions\nshouted by a crewmember.\nDECOLLAGE/ATERRISSAGE\n• You do not have the visual capacity to assess conditions\noutside of the exit or pertorm any other tunction described\nwithout the assistance of visual aids other than contact\nlenses or eyeglasses.\nIn the event ot an emergency, tollow the directions and nand\nsignals of your crew. If a crewmember is not available to\nassist vou, tollow the instructions on the Satety Instructions\ncard and posted signs. Wait until the airplane has stopped\nbefore opening the exit and look through the window,\nassessing conditions (looking for smoke, fire or obstructions)\nto determine whether it is safe to proceed. If it is safe to\ndo so, operate the exit and assist others according to the\ninstructions. Assess, select and follow a safe path away\nfrom the airplane.\nYour Flight Attendants will be glad to answer any questions\nvou may nave",
      "EVACUATION SUR L'EAU\nR\n6)\nCopyright © 1989 US Airways\n757-2-ECPS\nC/C 190-4850\nRev. 6/97\n2002.127.653"
